{"name":"Private Jet","hex":"#889db2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"private","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging or pertaining to an individual person, group of people, or entity that is not the state.","Relating to an individual or group of individuals outside of their official roles; often, sensitive or personal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soldier of the lowest rank in the army.","A doctor working in privately rather than publicly funded health care."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/private"},{"term":"jet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Manem."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A collimated stream, spurt or flow of liquid or gas from a pressurized container, an engine, etc.","A spout or nozzle for creating a jet of fluid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Business jet","blocks":[{"text":"A business jet, private jet, or bizjet is a jet aircraft designed for transporting small groups of people, typically business executives and high-ranking associates. Business jets are generally designed for faster air travel and more personal comfort than commercial aircraft, and may be adapted for other roles, such as casualty evacuation or express parcel deliveries, and some are used by public bodies, government officials, VIPs, or even the military."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/OO-FLN.JPG/330px-OO-FLN.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Business_jet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Lounge_2_%286749182849%29.jpg/500px-Lounge_2_%286749182849%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Lounge_2_%286749182849%29.jpg/1280px-Lounge_2_%286749182849%29.jpg?utm_source=en